{
  "title": "Solving Equations by Graphing",
  "description": "Solve one-variable equations in Desmos by getting zero on one side, graphing the other side, and reading the x-intercepts.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "try_the_radical",
      "html": "<h2>Give it a try</h2><p>Spend about a minute on this equation. Keep what you tried, even if you got stuck.</p>",
      "shared_prompt": {
        "id": "opening_radical",
        "title": "Opening problem",
        "html": "<p>Solve \\(\\sqrt{x+4}+\\sqrt{x-1}=5\\).</p>"
      },
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "why_start_with_the_radical",
      "html": "<h2>When the algebra gets messy</h2><p>How did that go? Those two square roots show how much work an equation can take by hand. A graph can get you to the answer faster.</p><p>We’ll try it on \\(x+5=0\\) first so you can see what to look for, then come back to the square roots.</p>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "graph_the_line",
      "block_type": "desmos_interactive",
      "content": {
        "type": "desmos_interactive",
        "title": "Graph the expression",
        "instructions_html": "<p>Type \\(x+5\\) in Desmos, then select <strong>Check Answer</strong>.</p>",
        "initial_expressions": [],
        "goal": {
          "type": "enter_expression",
          "required_count": 1
        },
        "validation": {
          "mode": "equivalent",
          "expected": [
            "x+5"
          ],
          "test_values": [
            -5,
            -2,
            0,
            2
          ],
          "state_rules": {
            "min_expressions": 1,
            "max_expressions": 1,
            "require_visible_only": true
          }
        },
        "feedback": {
          "success_message_html": "<p>Nice work! You graphed \\(x+5\\) correctly.</p>",
          "retry_message_html": "<p>Enter just the expression on the left of the equals sign.</p>",
          "reveal_solution_after_attempts": 3,
          "solution_html": "<p>Type \\(x+5\\) on the first row.</p>"
        },
        "progression": {
          "require_success": true
        }
      },
      "shared_prompt": {
        "id": "first_zero_equation",
        "title": "Equation to solve",
        "html": "<p>\\(x+5=0\\)</p>"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "why_look_at_the_x_axis",
      "html": "<h2>Why look at the x-axis?</h2><p>The graph’s height shows the value of \\(x+5\\). To solve \\(x+5=0\\), look on the x-axis, where that height is zero.</p><p>A point where the graph meets the x-axis is an <strong>x-intercept</strong>. Its x-coordinate is the solution.</p>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "find_zero_on_the_line",
      "block_type": "check",
      "content": {
        "prompt": "Click where the graph meets the x-axis. What is the x-coordinate?",
        "input": "numeric",
        "answer": "-5",
        "allow_retry": true,
        "hint": "The x-axis is horizontal. Read the first number in the point Desmos labels.",
        "explanation": "The x-intercept is \\((-5,0)\\), so the solution is \\(x=-5\\)."
      },
      "shared_prompt": "first_zero_equation",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "open",
        "mode": "preset",
        "title": "Read the x-intercept",
        "initial_expressions": [
          {
            "id": "row_1",
            "latex": "x+5"
          }
        ],
        "editable": false,
        "resettable": true
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "state_the_zero_side_rule",
      "html": "<h2>When one side is already zero</h2><p>You can go straight to the graph.</p><ol><li>Graph the expression on the other side.</li><li>Read the x-coordinate of every x-intercept.</li></ol>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "graph_the_quadratic",
      "block_type": "desmos_interactive",
      "content": {
        "type": "desmos_interactive",
        "title": "Try the same move",
        "instructions_html": "<p>Graph the left side of the equation.</p>",
        "initial_expressions": [],
        "goal": {
          "type": "enter_expression",
          "required_count": 1
        },
        "validation": {
          "mode": "equivalent",
          "expected": [
            "x^2+5x-6"
          ],
          "test_values": [
            -8,
            -6,
            -2,
            1,
            4
          ],
          "state_rules": {
            "min_expressions": 1,
            "max_expressions": 1,
            "require_visible_only": true
          }
        },
        "feedback": {
          "success_message_html": "<p>You got it! You graphed the left side.</p>",
          "retry_message_html": "<p>Include all three terms on the left side.</p>",
          "reveal_solution_after_attempts": 3,
          "solution_html": "<p>Type \\(x^2+5x-6\\).</p>"
        },
        "progression": {
          "require_success": true
        }
      },
      "shared_prompt": {
        "id": "first_quadratic",
        "title": "Equation to solve",
        "html": "<p>\\(x^2+5x-6=0\\)</p>"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "read_both_quadratic_roots",
      "block_type": "check",
      "content": {
        "prompt": "Find every x-intercept. What are the solutions?",
        "choices": [
          "\\(x=-1\\) and \\(x=6\\)",
          "\\(x=-6\\) and \\(x=1\\)",
          "\\(x=0\\) and \\(x=1\\)",
          "\\(x=-6\\) only"
        ],
        "correct_index": 1,
        "allow_retry": true,
        "hint": "Look on both sides of the origin. Read the first coordinate at each intercept.",
        "explanation": "The x-intercepts give two solutions, \\(x=-6\\) and \\(x=1\\)."
      },
      "shared_prompt": "first_quadratic",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "open",
        "mode": "preset",
        "title": "Read both x-intercepts",
        "initial_expressions": [
          {
            "id": "row_1",
            "latex": "x^2+5x-6"
          }
        ],
        "editable": false,
        "resettable": true
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "explain_variable_change",
      "html": "<h2>What if the equation uses a different letter?</h2><p>Desmos uses \\(x\\) for the horizontal axis. If the equation uses \\(t\\), replace it with \\(x\\) to graph. When you report your solutions, call them \\(t\\)-values.</p>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "rename_for_desmos",
      "block_type": "desmos_interactive",
      "content": {
        "type": "desmos_interactive",
        "title": "Graph using x",
        "instructions_html": "<p>Graph the left side with \\(x\\) in place of \\(t\\).</p>",
        "initial_expressions": [],
        "goal": {
          "type": "enter_expression",
          "required_count": 1
        },
        "validation": {
          "mode": "equivalent",
          "expected": [
            "x^2-5x+4"
          ],
          "test_values": [
            -2,
            0,
            1,
            4,
            5
          ],
          "state_rules": {
            "min_expressions": 1,
            "max_expressions": 1,
            "require_visible_only": true
          }
        },
        "feedback": {
          "success_message_html": "<p>Nice work! You used \\(x\\) in place of \\(t\\).</p>",
          "retry_message_html": "<p>Replace each t with x and graph just the expression on the left.</p>",
          "reveal_solution_after_attempts": 3,
          "solution_html": "<p>Enter \\(x^2-5x+4\\).</p>"
        },
        "progression": {
          "require_success": true
        }
      },
      "shared_prompt": {
        "id": "other_variable",
        "title": "Equation in t",
        "html": "<p>\\(t^2-5t+4=0\\)</p>"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "report_the_original_letter",
      "block_type": "check",
      "content": {
        "prompt": "Read the x-intercepts. What are the solutions to the original equation?",
        "choices": [
          "\\(x=1\\) and \\(x=4\\)",
          "\\(t=-1\\) and \\(t=-4\\)",
          "\\(t=0\\) only",
          "\\(t=1\\) and \\(t=4\\)"
        ],
        "correct_index": 3,
        "allow_retry": true,
        "hint": "Keep the values you read from the graph and use the letter in the original equation.",
        "explanation": "The graph gives \\(1\\) and \\(4\\). Report them as \\(t=1\\) and \\(t=4\\)."
      },
      "shared_prompt": "other_variable",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "open",
        "mode": "preset",
        "title": "Read x, report t",
        "initial_expressions": [
          {
            "id": "row_1",
            "latex": "x^2-5x+4"
          }
        ],
        "editable": false,
        "resettable": true
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "explain_rewriting_to_zero",
      "html": "<h2>What if neither side is zero?</h2><p>Move every term to one side, changing the sign of each term you move. That leaves zero on the other side.</p><p>Now it’s in the same equals-zero form you already know how to solve. Graph the expression and read the x-intercepts.</p>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "make_one_side_zero",
      "block_type": "desmos_interactive",
      "content": {
        "type": "desmos_interactive",
        "title": "Get zero on one side",
        "instructions_html": "<p>Move \\(7x\\) to the left side, then graph that side.</p>",
        "initial_expressions": [],
        "goal": {
          "type": "enter_expression",
          "required_count": 1
        },
        "validation": {
          "mode": "equivalent",
          "expected": [
            "x^2-7x+12"
          ],
          "test_values": [
            -3,
            0,
            2,
            3,
            4,
            6
          ],
          "state_rules": {
            "min_expressions": 1,
            "max_expressions": 1,
            "require_visible_only": true
          }
        },
        "feedback": {
          "success_message_html": "<p>Exactly! You moved \\(7x\\) over and graphed the new left side.</p>",
          "retry_message_html": "<p>When \\(+7x\\) moves to the left, it becomes \\(-7x\\).</p>",
          "reveal_solution_after_attempts": 3,
          "solution_html": "<p>Move \\(7x\\) to the left to get \\(x^2-7x+12=0\\). Graph \\(x^2-7x+12\\).</p>"
        },
        "progression": {
          "require_success": true
        }
      },
      "shared_prompt": {
        "id": "terms_on_both_sides",
        "title": "Equation to solve",
        "html": "<p>\\(x^2+12=7x\\)</p>"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "read_solutions_after_rewrite",
      "block_type": "check",
      "content": {
        "prompt": "Read the x-intercepts. Which values solve the equation?",
        "choices": [
          "\\(x=3\\) and \\(x=4\\)",
          "\\(x=-3\\) and \\(x=-4\\)",
          "\\(x=0\\) and \\(x=7\\)",
          "\\(x=4\\) only"
        ],
        "correct_index": 0,
        "allow_retry": true,
        "hint": "Read each x-coordinate where the graph meets the horizontal axis.",
        "explanation": "The x-intercepts give \\(x=3\\) and \\(x=4\\)."
      },
      "shared_prompt": "terms_on_both_sides",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "open",
        "mode": "preset",
        "title": "Find both solutions",
        "initial_expressions": [
          {
            "id": "row_1",
            "latex": "x^2-7x+12"
          }
        ],
        "editable": false,
        "resettable": true
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "assemble_the_full_routine",
      "html": "<h2>Zero, Graph, Click</h2><ol><li><strong>Zero.</strong> Move all the terms to one side, leaving zero on the other.</li><li><strong>Graph.</strong> Type the other side in Desmos, using \\(x\\) for the variable.</li><li><strong>Click.</strong> Read the x-coordinate of every x-intercept. Report the solutions using the original variable.</li></ol><p>Try these three moves on the opening problem.</p>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "return_to_the_radical",
      "block_type": "desmos_interactive",
      "content": {
        "type": "desmos_interactive",
        "title": "Return to the opening problem",
        "instructions_html": "<p>Remember this one? It looked like a lot of algebra at the start. Try it again with <strong>Zero, Graph, Click</strong>.</p>",
        "initial_expressions": [],
        "goal": {
          "type": "enter_expression",
          "required_count": 1
        },
        "validation": {
          "mode": "equivalent",
          "expected": [
            "\\sqrt{x+4}+\\sqrt{x-1}-5",
            "5-\\sqrt{x+4}-\\sqrt{x-1}"
          ],
          "test_values": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            5,
            9,
            16
          ],
          "state_rules": {
            "min_expressions": 1,
            "max_expressions": 1,
            "require_visible_only": true
          }
        },
        "feedback": {
          "success_message_html": "<p>You did it! You set up the opening problem for the x-intercept method.</p>",
          "retry_message_html": "<p>Think back to the first move. How can you leave zero on one side?</p>",
          "reveal_solution_after_attempts": 3,
          "solution_html": "<p>Enter \\(\\sqrt{x+4}+\\sqrt{x-1}-5\\).</p>"
        },
        "progression": {
          "require_success": true
        }
      },
      "shared_prompt": "opening_radical"
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "confirm_the_radical_solution",
      "block_type": "check",
      "content": {
        "prompt": "Click the x-intercept. What value of \\(x\\) solves the opening equation?",
        "input": "numeric",
        "answer": "5",
        "allow_retry": true,
        "hint": "Use the first coordinate of the point on the x-axis.",
        "explanation": "The x-intercept gives \\(x=5\\). Compare that with your first try. One subtraction and a graph got you to the answer."
      },
      "shared_prompt": "opening_radical",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "open",
        "mode": "preset",
        "title": "Read the x-intercept",
        "initial_expressions": [
          {
            "id": "row_1",
            "latex": "\\sqrt{x+4}+\\sqrt{x-1}-5"
          }
        ],
        "editable": false,
        "resettable": true
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "explain_matching_exact_choices",
      "html": "<h2>When the choices are exact</h2><p>Desmos may label an x-intercept with a decimal. If the answer choices are exact expressions, type them in Desmos and pick the one whose decimal matches the intercept.</p>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "hard_radical_setup",
      "block_type": "desmos_interactive",
      "content": {
        "type": "desmos_interactive",
        "title": "Set up the graph",
        "instructions_html": "<p>Get zero on one side and graph the other side using \\(x\\).</p>",
        "initial_expressions": [],
        "goal": {
          "type": "enter_expression",
          "required_count": 1
        },
        "validation": {
          "mode": "equivalent",
          "expected": [
            "2+\\sqrt{x+9}-x",
            "-\\left(2+\\sqrt{x+9}-x\\right)"
          ],
          "test_values": [
            -8,
            -2,
            0,
            2,
            5,
            9
          ],
          "state_rules": {
            "min_expressions": 1,
            "max_expressions": 1,
            "require_visible_only": true
          }
        },
        "feedback": {
          "success_message_html": "<p>Nice work! You handled the new variable and got zero on one side.</p>",
          "retry_message_html": "<p>Use x for r. Move the right side to the left, outside the radical.</p>",
          "reveal_solution_after_attempts": 3,
          "solution_html": "<p>Enter \\(2+\\sqrt{x+9}-x\\).</p>"
        },
        "progression": {
          "require_success": true
        }
      },
      "shared_prompt": {
        "id": "exact_radical_transfer",
        "title": "Equation to solve",
        "html": "<p>Solve \\(2+\\sqrt{r+9}=r\\). Give the exact value of \\(r\\).</p>"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "match_the_exact_radical",
      "block_type": "check",
      "content": {
        "prompt": "Compare the choices in Desmos. Which one matches the x-intercept?",
        "choices": [
          "\\(\\dfrac{5-3\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\)",
          "\\(\\dfrac{3+5\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\)",
          "\\(\\dfrac{5+3\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\)",
          "\\(\\dfrac{5+\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\)"
        ],
        "correct_index": 2,
        "allow_retry": true,
        "hint": "Type each choice on its own row. Use the fraction template to keep the whole numerator over \\(2\\).",
        "explanation": "The intercept is about \\(5.854\\). The choice \\((5+3\\sqrt{5})/2\\) rounds to the same number."
      },
      "shared_prompt": "exact_radical_transfer",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "open",
        "mode": "preset",
        "title": "Compare exact choices",
        "initial_expressions": [
          {
            "id": "row_1",
            "latex": "2+\\sqrt{x+9}-x"
          }
        ],
        "editable": true,
        "resettable": true
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "explain_counting_intercepts",
      "html": "<h2>When the question asks how many</h2><p>Count the x-intercepts. A point counts even if the graph only touches the x-axis. Each different x-coordinate gives one distinct solution.</p>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "hard_quartic_setup",
      "block_type": "desmos_interactive",
      "content": {
        "type": "desmos_interactive",
        "title": "Set up the graph",
        "instructions_html": "<p>Get zero on one side and graph the other side.</p>",
        "initial_expressions": [],
        "goal": {
          "type": "enter_expression",
          "required_count": 1
        },
        "validation": {
          "mode": "equivalent",
          "expected": [
            "x^4-4x^2+4",
            "-\\left(x^4-4x^2+4\\right)"
          ],
          "test_values": [
            -3,
            -2,
            -1,
            0,
            1,
            2,
            3
          ],
          "state_rules": {
            "min_expressions": 1,
            "max_expressions": 1,
            "require_visible_only": true
          }
        },
        "feedback": {
          "success_message_html": "<p>You got it! That’s the expression to use for finding the x-intercepts.</p>",
          "retry_message_html": "<p>Try moving \\(4x^2\\) to the left side.</p>",
          "reveal_solution_after_attempts": 3,
          "solution_html": "<p>Enter \\(x^4-4x^2+4\\).</p>"
        },
        "progression": {
          "require_success": true
        }
      },
      "shared_prompt": {
        "id": "quartic_transfer",
        "title": "Equation to solve",
        "html": "<p>How many distinct real solutions does \\(x^4+4=4x^2\\) have?</p>"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "count_quartic_touches",
      "block_type": "check",
      "content": {
        "prompt": "Count the x-intercepts. How many solutions are there?",
        "input": "numeric",
        "answer": "2",
        "allow_retry": true,
        "hint": "Look for any point where the graph meets the horizontal axis.",
        "explanation": "The graph touches the x-axis at two different points, so there are two distinct real solutions."
      },
      "shared_prompt": "quartic_transfer",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "open",
        "mode": "preset",
        "title": "Count the x-intercepts",
        "initial_expressions": [
          {
            "id": "row_1",
            "latex": "x^4-4x^2+4"
          }
        ],
        "editable": false,
        "resettable": true
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "raw_block",
      "id": "recall_the_method",
      "block_type": "check",
      "content": {
        "prompt": "A friend is stuck on an equation in \\(p\\). How would you explain Zero, Graph, Click?",
        "choices": [
          "Set one side to zero, graph the other in x, and report each intercept’s x-coordinate as a p-value.",
          "Set one side to zero, graph the other in x, and report its y-intercept as the p-value.",
          "Graph both sides separately and report where either graph meets the x-axis.",
          "Graph the difference in x and report only where it crosses the axis as p-values."
        ],
        "correct_index": 0,
        "allow_retry": false,
        "explanation": "Get zero on one side and graph the other in \\(x\\). Each x-intercept gives you a solution to report in \\(p\\)."
      },
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "homework_start",
      "html": "<h2>Try it on your own</h2><p>Try these four questions now or save them for homework. Select <strong>Reset</strong> in Desmos between questions.</p>",
      "calculator": {
        "display": "hidden"
      }
    },
    {
